  "notes": [
    "The Wongs' ADL day inside seen-home-wong (HOME-PLAN §5.2), for scripts/build-community-tracks.mjs (schema: docs/COMMUNITY.md, Cast files). Loop seconds (720 s = 8 AM-4 PM).",
    "Positions are facility-local (plan frame P, +x east, +z north, metres); headings follow three.js (heading h faces (sin h, cos h)). `at` is a seat object (chairs and benches: seatPose) or a point with `heading`; `seat` names the furniture a seated point sits on, exempt from the furniture-clearance check.",
    "Each stop is a stationary hold over `window`; the gap to the next stop (or to an away/leave time) is the walk at the person's `gait` (metres per loop second), with 1.5-2 s of slack so the generator can stagger people. Consecutive stops at the same place change only the action or title.",
    "`arrive`/`leave` are front-door passes (the `door` anchor), staggered at least 2 s apart; `away` windows go out and back through it. Mrs. Wong arrives at her bed at 0.5 s (the loop seam out of sight) and leaves at 720 s (present to the end); Mr. Wong rolls in at 672 s. Time outside is a hole filled by HOLE_LEGS in community-people.ts (the clinic trip, the aide's car and porch, the visitors' arrivals, Mr. Wong's hospital day).",
    "An `interaction` is defined once, on one stop: actors = the person plus `with`; `window` defaults to the stop window. Ids kept stable: home-personal-care (30-72), home-health-visit (683.5-700), after-hours-call (690-708), home-return, home-meals, home-mods, home-discharge-arrival. home-van-boarding and home-pill-drop stay outdoors in community-people.ts.",
    "Mr. Wong keeps his wheelchair all day (no per-segment mobility override yet), so the nurse checks his transfer technique beside the armchair instead of moving him into it."
  ],
